---
// The full gates chapter (story prototype, chapter 2): pipeline animation, event log and gate cards. Shown on /security/.
import { PIPE } from '../../lib/landing-svg';
interface Props { chapter?: string | null }
const { chapter = '2' } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="band alt" id="gates" aria-labelledby="ch2">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chap-head">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="pip"></span>{chapter && <>Chapter {chapter} <span class="sep">·</span> </>}The gates</span>
      <p class="kicker">It should never have gotten in.</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="ch2">Six gates between the internet and your build.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Each one is a feature of the registry, not a bolt-on. Packages that fail are refused with a real HTTP status your package manager understands.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pipe screen" id="pipe">
      <div class="screen-bar"><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="crumb">proxy <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> <b>upstream to build</b></span><span class="right"><span class="pill blue">6 gates</span></span></div>
      <div class="pipe-screen">
        <div class="pipe-scroll"><div class="pipe-inner">
          <svg class="pipe-svg" id="pipesvg" viewBox="0 0 1200 150" role="img" aria-label="Pipeline: Upstream, Age gate, Curation, Scan, Policy, Quality gate, Promote, Your builds.">
            <defs><linearGradient id="pipegrad" x1="0" x2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#087CF4"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#34D399"/></linearGradient></defs>
            <line class="track" x1="70" y1="56" x2="1130" y2="56"/>
            <line class="trackfill" id="trackfill" x1="70" y1="56" x2="1130" y2="56"/>
            <Fragment set:html={PIPE} />
            <g id="gpk"></g>
          </svg>
        </div></div>
        <p class="scroll-hint">scroll the pipeline sideways</p>
        <div class="glog-head"><span>Gate events</span><span class="tag">example events</span></div>
        <ol class="glog" id="glog">
          <li data-g="1"><span class="g">01 age gate</span><span class="pill amber">held</span><span class="msg">version published 2 days ago. Held until day 7.</span></li>
          <li data-g="2"><span class="g">02 curation</span><span class="pill red">blocked</span><span class="msg">matched rule <code>evil-*</code> (known-bad package family)</span></li>
          <li data-g="3"><span class="g">03 scan</span><span class="pill blue">graded</span><span class="msg">Trivy + Grype findings → A–F grade</span></li>
          <li data-g="4"><span class="g">04 policy</span><span class="pill red">403</span><span class="msg">Artifact download is blocked by the repository's scan policy</span></li>
          <li data-g="5"><span class="g">05 quality gate</span><span class="pill red">failed</span><span class="msg">health 61 &lt; min 75 · 1 critical &gt; max 0</span></li>
          <li data-g="6"><span class="g">06 promote</span><span class="pill green">promoted</span><span class="msg">staging → release · gate_results recorded</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gates" id="gatecards">
      <article class="card gate" data-g="1">
        <div class="top"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="8"/><path d="M12 9v4l2.5 2M10 2h4"/></svg></span><div><div class="idx">GATE 01</div><h3>Age gate</h3></div></div>
        <p>Holds new upstream versions on proxy repositories until they are old enough. npm, PyPI and Go module proxies. Measured by upstream publish time or first seen.</p>
        <div class="cfg">enabled: true · min_age_days: 7</div>
        <div class="out"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg>version published 2 days ago. Held until day 7.</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card gate" data-g="2">
        <div class="top"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16l-6 7v6l-4 2v-8z"/></svg></span><div><div class="idx">GATE 02</div><h3>Curation</h3></div></div>
        <p>Pattern rules, publisher-trust rules, a review queue and global baselines. New packages land as pending, approved, blocked or review.</p>
        <div class="cfg">package_pattern: "evil-*" · action: block</div>
        <div class="out"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M5.6 5.6l12.8 12.8"/></svg>blocked: matched rule evil-* (known-bad package family)</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card gate" data-g="3">
        <div class="top"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="M20 20l-3.5-3.5M8 11h6"/></svg></span><div><div class="idx">GATE 03</div><h3>Scan</h3></div></div>
        <p>Trivy, Grype, OpenSCAP and Dependency-Track. Results are cached by content hash, so a blob is scanned once.</p>
        <div class="cfg">Trivy + Grype → A–F grade</div>
        <div class="out okc"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg>findings → A–F grade</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card gate" data-g="4">
        <div class="top"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l8 4v5c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V7z"/></svg></span><div><div class="idx">GATE 04</div><h3>Policy</h3></div></div>
        <p>Block, warn, allow or quarantine. Per repository or global, in YAML or JSON. Origin policies gate proxied content too.</p>
        <div class="cfg">action: block · denied_upstreams: [...]</div>
        <div class="out"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M5.6 5.6l12.8 12.8"/></svg>403 Artifact download is blocked by the repository's scan policy</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card gate" data-g="5">
        <div class="top"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 20V10M10 20V4M16 20v-7M22 20H2"/></svg></span><div><div class="idx">GATE 05</div><h3>Quality gate</h3></div></div>
        <p>A health score from 0 to 100, graded A to F, checked before policy.</p>
        <div class="weights" aria-hidden="true"><i style="width:40%;background:var(--accent)"></i><i style="width:25%;background:var(--accent2)"></i><i style="width:20%;background:var(--ok)"></i><i style="width:15%;background:var(--warn)"></i></div>
        <div class="weights-l"><span>security 40%</span><span>quality 25%</span><span>license 20%</span><span>metadata 15%</span></div>
        <div class="cfg">min_health_score: 75 · max_critical_issues: 0</div>
        <div class="out"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M5.6 5.6l12.8 12.8"/></svg>health 61 &lt; min 75 · 1 critical &gt; max 0</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card gate" data-g="6">
        <div class="top"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20V5M6 11l6-6 6 6"/></svg></span><div><div class="idx">GATE 06</div><h3>Promote</h3></div></div>
        <p>Staging to release, behind CVE and license gates. Every gate rule is recorded with the promotion.</p>
        <div class="cfg">gate_results: [&#123;rule, passed, reason&#125;]</div>
        <div class="out okc"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg>staging → release</div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
